{"id":"shield","name":"Shield","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:shield"],"groups":["Figurative"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Shield","text":"Used in defensive warfare, varying at different times and under different circumstances in size, form, and material (1 Sam. 17:7; 2 Sam. 1:21; 1 Kings 10:17; 1 Chr. 12:8, 24, 34; Isa. 22:6; Ezek. 39:9; Nahum 2:3). Used figuratively of God and of earthly princes as the defenders of their people (Gen. 15:1; Deut. 33:29; Ps. 33:20; 84:11). Faith is compared to a shield (Eph. 6:16). Shields were usually “anointed” (Isa. 21:5), in order to preserve them, and at the same time make the missiles of the enemy glide off them more easily."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4043","lemma":"מָגֵן","xlit":"mâgên","gloss":"a shield","kjv":"armed, buckler, defence, ruler","count":29,"share":0.76},{"strong":"H6793","lemma":"צִנָּה","xlit":"tsinnâh","gloss":"a hook","kjv":"buckler, cold, hook, shield","count":10,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H7820","lemma":"שָׁחַט","xlit":"shâchaṭ","gloss":"to hammer out","kjv":"beat","count":4,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H7420","lemma":"רֹמַח","xlit":"rômach","gloss":"a lance","kjv":"buckler, javelin, lancet, spear","count":4,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H2091","lemma":"זָהָב","xlit":"zâhâb","gloss":"gold, figuratively, something gold-colored , as oil, a c","kjv":"gold, fair weather","count":6,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H3468","lemma":"יֶשַׁע","xlit":"yeshaʻ","gloss":"liberty, deliverance, prosperity","kjv":"safety, salvation, saving","count":4,"share":0.11}],"verses":["Gen.15.1","Deut.33.29","2Sam.1.21","2Sam.22.3","2Sam.22.36","1Kgs.10.17","1Kgs.14.27","2Chr.9.16","2Chr.14.8","2Chr.17.17","2Chr.23.9","2Chr.26.14","2Chr.32.5","2Chr.32.27","Job.15.26","Ps.18.2","Ps.18.35","Ps.33.20","Ps.35.2","Ps.59.11","Ps.84.9","Ps.84.11","Ps.89.18","Prov.30.5","Isa.22.6","Jer.46.3","Ezek.38.4","Ezek.39.9","Nah.2.3","2Sam.8.7","1Kgs.10.16","1Kgs.17.0","2Kgs.11.10","2Chr.9.15","2Chr.11.12","Ps.5.12","Ps.91.4","Ezek.3